# Inputs driven (Wokwi MCP), in order
# note: the Wokwi sim fast-forwards tens of seconds of sim time between tool
# calls, so a held button (across two calls) always exceeds the 1 s long-press
# threshold, and a same-message press+release lands below the 15 ms debounce
# window. A controlled sub-second "short press" (SPIN/SELECT) was therefore not
# reliably producible from the MCP tools.

t~2.8s   sim started, attract mode
         read uno pin13 (CLK)  -> false  (SPI idle low, mode 0)  OK
         read uno pin10 (CS)   -> true   (CS idle high)          OK
         read uno pin9  (BUZZ) -> false  (silent in attract)     OK
btnA pressed=1        (held)
t~66s    (held ~63 s of sim time -> registers as a LONG press, ignored in attract)
btnA pressed=0        (release: long_fired -> no SHORT event)
btnA pressed=1 / =0   (same message, dwell < debounce -> likely no event)
btnA pressed=1 / =0   (same message, retry)
         read uno pin9 x4 -> false,false,false,false (no tone caught)
t~218s   sim still running, stable, no fault/reset
         added wokwi-logic-analyzer to diagram, restarted sim
         MCP server disconnected before VCD capture / further driving
